+# Bridge Work Order — guard(ops): wire redis_quota_monitor into a scheduler (#1839)
+
+**Lane**: coder → admin (`.github/` apply + 2 secrets). **Delivered**: 2 code files
+(`scripts/ops/redis_quota_monitor.py` persistent-state patch, `tests/test_redis_quota_monitor.py`
++3 tests) and this runbook carrying the VERBATIM scheduled workflow (§3) — agents cannot write
+protected paths (#1643 precedent).
+
+## The finding (verified live this run, dual-source)
+
+`scripts/ops/redis_quota_monitor.py` (landed via #1779, the #1698 D1 lane) is a complete,
+tested Telegram alerting monitor for the Upstash chain — **wired to nothing**:
+
+- No scheduler anywhere references it (the audit's repo-wide grep, 2026-10-28 07:50+08 dispatch;
+  the only in-tree mention is its `_INDEX.md` doc line).
+- **State-file defect compounds it**: the default state path lived in
+  `tempfile.gettempdir()` → on any ephemeral host the alert dedup + `[BURN]` two-run history
+  evaporate on every restart, so the burn projection can NEVER engage (its own honest skip:
+  "insufficient history").
+- Live consequence: primary **480000/500000 (96%, soft-threshold hit)**, secondary identical,
+  tertiary active — `redis_rotation_status` 2026-10-28T00:26Z, matching the filing audit
+  number-for-number. Window resets **2026-11-01T00:01Z** (~3.6 days). Per the monitor's own
+  doctrine, `crit` alerts should be reaching Telegram — none ever will until scheduled.
+
+## §1 What this patch changes (code, agent-lane)
+
+1. `default_state_path()` — new home-relative default `~/.supremeai/redis_quota_alert_state.json`
+   (`REDIS_QUOTA_STATE_FILE` override still wins). `/tmp` is now never the default.
+2. `save_state()` — creates missing parent dirs (`os.makedirs(exist_ok=True)`) so a fresh host
+   with no `~/.supremeai` does not fail silently.
+3. Self-test +2 checks (default-outside-tmp contract, parent-dir creation); pytest +3 tests
+   (same contracts + env-override precedence). 30/30 PASS, 45 self-test PASS, `py_compile` PASS.
+
+## §2 Admin checklist (3 minutes)
+
+1. **Secrets (do not exist yet — verified `github_list_secrets` 2026-10-28T00:26Z, 13 secrets,
+   none TELEGRAM_*):**
+   - `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` — the operator alert bot's token (same bot the tower's
+     `notify_send_telegram` uses).
+   - `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` — the operator alert chat's numeric id (same chat the tower posts to).
+2. **Workflow**: create `.github/workflows/redis-quota-monitor.yml` with EXACTLY the §3 content.
+3. **Prove the wiring**: Actions tab → `redis-quota-monitor` → Run workflow. Expect exit green,
+   log line `monitor exit 0` (or `1`/`2` if an alert fired — then check Telegram received it).
+   Do NOT fabricate usage to force an alert (U2 honesty tiering, per the #1839 never-do register).
+
+## §3 Verbatim workflow (admin applies as-is)
+
+```yaml
+name: redis-quota-monitor
+
+on:
+  schedule:
+    # every 30 min at :13/:43 UTC — burn-rate math needs frequent snapshots;
+    # the state file already dedups alerts per (account, tier, window)
+    - cron: "13,43 * * * *"
+  workflow_dispatch: {}
+
+permissions:
+  contents: read
+
+jobs:
+  monitor:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    timeout-minutes: 5
+    steps:
+      - name: Checkout monorepo mirror
+        uses: actions/checkout@11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683 # v4.2.2 (SHA-pinned per #1776/R35)
+
+      - name: Set up Python
+        uses: actions/setup-python@0a5c61591373683505ea898e09a3ea4f39ef2b9c # v5.3.0
+        with:
+          python-version: "3.11"
+
+      - name: Restore alert state (persistent [BURN] history)
+        uses: actions/cache@1bd1e32a3bdc45362d1e726936510720a7c30a57 # v4.2.0
+        with:
+          path: ~/.supremeai
+          key: rqm-state-${{ github.run_id }}
+          restore-keys: |
+            rqm-state-
+
+      - name: Run quota monitor (live; alerts -> Telegram)
+        id: rqm
+        env:
+          SUPREMEAI_TOWER_URL: https://supremeai-mcp-tower.onrender.com/mcp
+          TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN }}
+          TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID: ${{ secrets.TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID }}
+        run: |
+          code=0
+          python scripts/ops/redis_quota_monitor.py || code=$?
+          echo "rqm_exit=$code" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+          if [ "$code" -ge 3 ]; then exit "$code"; fi
+          echo "monitor exit $code (0=no alert, 1=warn sent, 2=crit sent) — delivery channel is Telegram"
+          exit 0
+```
+
+## §4 Behavior contract
+
+- **Exit 0** — evaluated, nothing to alert (or honest skip printed); job green.
+- **Exit 1 / 2** — warn/crit alert DELIVERED to Telegram; job stays green **by design**:
+  during a sustained 96%-crit window (the current one runs to Nov 1) red CI every 30 min
+  would train operators to ignore red. The action channel is Telegram; CI is only the
+  scheduler. The exit code is recorded in `rqm_exit` for anyone wiring stricter policy later.
+- **Exit ≥ 3** — strict-mode fetch failure (tower unreachable with `REDIS_QUOTA_STRICT=1`)
+  or hard error → job RED (a monitor that cannot see must be visible).
+- **Cache honesty**: GitHub cache is LRU (7-day disuse, 10 GB/repo). If evicted, `[BURN]`
+  history restarts — the monitor's own honest skip handles it (no fabricated projections);
+  dedup state loss at worst re-sends one alert per (account, tier, window).
+- **No pushes, no merges, no satellite writes** — the job reads the tower's
+  `redis_rotation_status` and posts to Telegram. That is all.
+
+## §5 Validation performed (this submission)
+
+- `py_compile` PASS (both files); unittest 30/30 (27 pre-existing unmodified + 3 new);
+  monitor `--self-test` 45 PASS / 0 FAIL (43 pre-existing + 2 new #1839 checks).
+- Live cross-check: `redis_rotation_status` 2026-10-28T00:26Z = primary/secondary 96% crit,
+  tertiary active — the exact state the monitor must start reporting to Telegram.
+- Secret scan of all delivered files: CLEAN (token/chat referenced by env names only).
+- `.github/` untouched by this PR (§3 is the only workflow source of truth, printed above).
+
+## §6 Rollback
+
+Delete `.github/workflows/redis-quota-monitor.yml` (unschedules instantly; the monitor
+reverts to manual runs). Reverting the code patch restores the `/tmp` default byte-for-byte;
+neither step touches production Redis or the Telegram bot.
